<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's coffee exports drop 20.2 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's coffee exports drop 20.2 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's coffee exports fell 20.2 percent in 1996 because of lower production and more of the crop was retained in the country.</p>
<p>According to figures released Wednesday by the National Association of Coffee Exporters, exports in 1996 totalled 1.56 million 60-kilo bags, compared with 1.95 million bags in 1995.</p>
<p>Ecuador put a limit on its coffee exports since the middle of 1995 in order to try to achieve higher prices.</p>
<p>The Association of Coffee Exporting Countries have agreed to limit combined Ecuadorean and Central American coffee exports at 8.7 million 60-kilo bags bewteen July 1996 and June 1997.</p>
<p>((--Franz Bastidas, Redaccion Quito, (5932) 258429))</p>
